# Tailwind CSS v4

Tailwind is configured **exclusively in `src/app/globals.css`** via `@theme`, `@plugin`, and `@custom-variant` directives. There is **no `tailwind.config.ts`** and there should never be one.

## Adding design tokens

Tokens are HSL-based CSS variables under `:root` and `.dark`, then mapped to Tailwind utility tokens inside `@theme`:

```css
:root {
  --background: 0 0% 100%;
}

@theme {
  --color-background: hsl(var(--background));
}
```

This makes `bg-background`, `text-background`, `border-background`, etc. available everywhere.

## Using tokens in components

```tsx
// ✅ DO — semantic tokens
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border border-border" />
<p className="text-muted-foreground" />

// ❌ DO NOT — hard-coded colours
<div className="bg-[#fff] text-[#000]" />
```

## Animations

Add keyframes inside `@theme` and reference via `--animate-*` tokens:

```css
@theme {
  --animate-shiny-text: shiny-text 8s infinite;
  @keyframes shiny-text { /* ... */ }
}
```

Then use `animate-shiny-text` as a class.

## Conditional classes

Always use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`:

```tsx
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

<div className={cn("flex items-center", isActive && "text-primary", className)} />
```

## Plugins

`tailwindcss-animate` is enabled via `@plugin 'tailwindcss-animate';` in `globals.css`. Don't add new plugins without updating that file.
